SUMMARY:[現場] Workshop with Saif Azzuz
LOCATION:O'Donohue Educational Farm
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/workshop-with-saif-azzuz
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53418724495078.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/work
 shop-with-saif-azzuz\n報名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/worksh
 op-with-saif-azzuz\n\nJoin us for an afternoon of artmaking with Saif Azzu
 z\, 2026-27 Doerr Visiting Artist\, and cultural fire practitioner Elizabe
 th Azzuz. In this all ages\, family friendly workshop\, the Azzuzs will sh
 are the significance of cultural fire\, or prescribed burns led by Indigen
 ous practitioners to steward healthy ecosystems. Participants will create 
 connections between native flora and fauna\, and make pigments and drawing
 s with charcoal from cultural fire burns.\n\nThis program takes place on t
 he O’Donohue Family Stanford Educational Farm at 555 Fremont Road\, Stan
 ford\, CA\, and is presented in conjunction with the Further Triennial exh
 ibition California Current\, on view at the Cantor from October 29\, 2026 
 through 2028\, which looks at the ecological\, infrastructural\, personal\
 , creative\, and activist networks that shape life in the region. Visit Ca
 lifornia Current to see works by Azzuz\, which include charcoal drawings m
 ade from similar processes.\n\nAll public programs at the Cantor Arts Cent
 er are always free! Space for this program is limited\; advance registrati
 on is recommended.\n\nRSVP here.\n\nAbout the Presenters\n\nSaif Azzuz (b.
  1987\, born in Eureka\, CA) is a Libyan-Yurok artist who resides in Pacif
 ica\, CA. He received a Bachelor’s Degree in Painting and Drawing from t
 he California College of the Arts in 2013. Working in painting\, sculpture
  and installation\, Azzuz’s work reimagines and examines our relationshi
 ps to nature\, privatization and commodification. The use of different med
 iums all
END:VEVENT
