SUMMARY:[現場]  Alexander Nemerov: The Work of Helen Frankenthaler
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center\, Cantor Eastman Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/alexander-nemerov-the-work-of-helen-f
 rankenthaler
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53418849977084.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/alex
 ander-nemerov-the-work-of-helen-frankenthaler\n報名/票券: https://thet
 hirdplace.is/event/alexander-nemerov-the-work-of-helen-frankenthaler\n\nWh
 at is the relationship between an artwork and its maker? Can we confidentl
 y link the two\, or do they diverge in meaning and intention? Join us for 
 a keynote lecture by Stanford Art History Professor Alexander Nemerov\, au
 thor of Fierce Poise: Helen Frankenthaler and 1950s New York\, as he refle
 cts on these enduring questions. Professor Nemerov will focus on the print
 s of Helen Frankenthaler\, which were recently gifted to the Cantor Arts C
 enter by the Helen Frankenthaler Foundation as part of a major exhibition 
 on the artist’s work\, to explore her groundbreaking legacy.\n\n​RSVP 
 here.\n\nAbout the Speaker:\n\nAlexander Nemerov\, the Carl and Marilynn T
 homa Professor in the Arts and Humanities at Stanford\, is the author of m
 any books\, including most recently Fierce Poise: Helen Frankenthaler and 
 1950s New York\, and another book called The Forest: A Fable of America in
  the 1830s\, which the novelist Annie Proulx called “one of the richest 
 books ever to come my way\, achingly painful and astonishingly tender.” 
 At Stanford\, Nemerov teaches a popular course called “How to Look at Ar
 t and Why."\n\nAll public programs at the Cantor Arts Center are always fr
 ee! Space for this program is limited\; advance registration is recommende
 d. Those who have registered will have priority for seating.\n\n________\n
 \nAccessibility Information or Requests\n\nCantor Arts Center at Stanford 
 University is committed to ensuring our programs are accessible to everyon
 e. To request access information and/or accommodations 
END:VEVENT
