SUMMARY:[現場] Time Doesn’t Stop: History\, Crisis\, and the Future of 
 Leftist Political Projects in South America
LOCATION:Bolivar House
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/el-tiempo-no-para-memoria-y-historia-
 para-pensar-proyectos-de-futuro-en-el-cono-sur
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53568260119599.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/el-t
 iempo-no-para-memoria-y-historia-para-pensar-proyectos-de-futuro-en-el-con
 o-sur\n\nCo-sponsored by the Consul General of Uruguay in San Francisco\n\
 nIn this lecture\, authors Aldo Marchesi y Vania Markarian will present th
 eir book El tiempo no para. The book aims to trace the history of the idea
  of human rights and to understand the impact of that concept on the devel
 opment of democracies at the close of the 20th century and in progressive 
 governments of the 21st century.  It further puts forth questions on the l
 imits of the language of human rights when considering the contemporary cr
 isis. \n\nAldo Marchesi holds a PhD in History from New York University an
 d is a Professor in the Department of Theory and Historiography at the Ins
 titute for History at The University of the Republic\, as well as a member
  of the Center for Uruguayan Interdisciplinary Studies. Together with coll
 eagues from other disciplines\, he recently founded the Institute for Rese
 arch on Social Justice and Inequality. He is a member of the National Syst
 em of Researchers in Uruguay. He has served as a visiting professor at uni
 versities and research centers in the United States\, Chile\, Argentina\, 
 Colombia\, and China. His work has focused on the recent history of Urugua
 y and the Southern Cone. He has published numerous articles and books. His
  first book\, reissued in 2023\, was El Uruguay Inventado: La política au
 diovisual durante la dictadura. His most recent book\, a regional history 
 of the armed Left in the Southern Cone\, was published in Spanish and Engl
 ish under the title Hacer la revolución (Maki
END:VEVENT
