DTSTAMP:20261012T113740Z
DTSTART:20261115T220000Z
DTEND:20261115T230000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Public Tour | Cantor Highlights in Chinese
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/copy-of-public-tour-cantor-highlights
 -in-chinese-4381
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53695215989203.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/copy
 -of-public-tour-cantor-highlights-in-chinese-4381\n\n在博物馆导览员
 的带领下，探索坎特艺术中心的收藏品。导览员将为您
 介绍来自不同文化和不同时期的精选作品。\n\n欢迎您参
 与对话，分享您对游览过程中所探讨主题的想法，或者
 按照自己的舒适程度参与互动。\n\n导览免费，但需提前
 登记。请通过以下链接选择并 RSVP 您希望参加的日期。\n
 \nSeptember 13\, 2026: https://thethirdplace.is/event/sept13\n\nOctober 11
 \, 2026: https://thethirdplace.is/event/oct11\n\nNovember 15\, 2026: https
 ://thethirdplace.is/event/nov15\n\n ______________________________________
 _____\n\n\n\nExplore the Cantor's collections with a museum engagement gui
 de who will lead you through a selection of works from different cultures 
 and time periods.\n\n Participants are welcomed to participate in the conv
 ersation and provide their thoughts on themes explored throughout the tour
  but are also free to engage at their own comfort level. \n\n Tours are fr
 ee of charge but require advance registration. Please select and RSVP for 
 your preferred date using the links below.\n\nSeptember 13\, 2026: https:/
 /thethirdplace.is/event/sept13\n\nOctober 11\, 2026: https://thethirdplace
 .is/event/oct11\n\nNovember 15\, 2026: https://thethirdplace.is/event/nov1
 5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-53727115437543@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20260817T162428Z
DTSTART:20261202T200000Z
DTEND:20261202T210000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] The Future of Health in Africa: How U.S. Presidential Deci
 sions Are Shaping a Generation of African Children - Dr. Ruth Gibson
LOCATION:Encina Commons\, Room 123
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-future-of-health-in-africa-how-us
 -presidential-decisions-are-shaping-a-generation-of-african-children-dr-ru
 th-gibson
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53727115437543.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/the-
 future-of-health-in-africa-how-us-presidential-decisions-are-shaping-a-gen
 eration-of-african-children-dr-ruth-gibson\n報名/票券: https://forms.g
 le/XQ2dYfcGygVDcNXZ9\n\nSession Description\n\nThe second Trump administra
 tion has undertaken a series of decisions with profound and lasting conseq
 uences for the health and survival of Africa’s children. The abrupt dism
 antling of the United States Agency for International Development (USAID) 
 is projected to result in approximately 14 million excess deaths\, the maj
 ority concentrated in sub-Saharan Africa. Concurrently\, the decision to i
 nitiate hostilities with Iran and the ensuing disruption of traffic throug
 h the Strait of Hormuz have severely constrained global fertilizer exports
  to African markets. Modeling informed by NASA agricultural forecasts indi
 cates that the 2027 growing season in the Sahel is at high risk of signifi
 cant production shortfalls and elevated famine risk. This talk presents on
 going research from the Stanford Geopolitical Human Impact Research Lab on
  the cascading effects of geopolitical decisions on human health. It focus
 es specifically on the projected impacts of the Strait of Hormuz crisis on
  food security and child nutrition across the Sahel in the 2027 season and
  outlines concrete policy options through which the United States can stil
 l act to avert a larger-scale humanitarian catastrophe.\n\nSpeaker Bio\n\n
 Dr. Ruth Gibson is the Founding Executive Director of the Stanford Geopoli
 tical Human Impact Research Lab\, the first research lab at Stanford Unive
 rsity dedicated to examining how geopolitical decisions shape human lives\
 , with particular attention to children. Based in the De
END:VEVENT
