SUMMARY:[現場] Digital Mirrors of Materiality
LOCATION:Anderson Collection\, Denning Family Resource Center
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/digital-mirrors-of-materiality
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53808344431532.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/digi
 tal-mirrors-of-materiality\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d
 /e/1FAIpQLSf9oEQbuYA6Q3OdZVyqOpz8lMLeu97FIc3o0pjMiFq3_rl_fQ/viewform?usp=h
 eader\n\npart of *Defying Boundaries: MacArthur Fellows at 45\n\nwith Kath
 erine Behar\, Nick Benson*\, Hideo Mabuchi*\, and Camille Utterback*\nMode
 rated by Vanessa Chang\n\nNovember 4\, 3:00-5:20PM\n\nDenning Family Resou
 rce Center\, Anderson Collection\n\nReception to follow\n5:30-6:30PM at th
 e McMurtry Building Courtyard\n\nWe are all in some way navigating widespr
 ead futureshock over paradigm-breaking growth in the power of computation 
 and robotics. Stepping back from the most expansive societal stakes to see
 k grounding at personal scale\, expressive making offers a rich context wi
 thin which to reflect upon what craft does for the maker\, and what is los
 t or gained when we augment or supplant embodied engagement with digital t
 echnologies. If our goal is not just to produce but to make things as a wa
 y of being at home in the world\, what could we possibly want from the lev
 erage of fabulous machines? Can traditional craft assimilate the expansive
 ness of the digital? How does this historical moment call for us to affirm
  the value of practicing heirloom modes of creativity?\n\n\nLearn more and
  RSVP\n****\n\nThis event made possible by John D. and Catherine T. MacArt
 hur Foundation \, Funding Good Chaos\, Stanford Arts Institute (SAI)\, the
  Department of Art and Art History  and the Office of the Vice President f
 or the Arts.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-53755962742429@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20260820T222418Z
DTSTART:20261116T210000Z
DTEND:20261116T220000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Curator Led Talk | surfacing
LOCATION:Anderson Collection\, Wisch Family Gallery
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/curator-led-talk-surfacing-nov
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53755962742429.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/cura
 tor-led-talk-surfacing-nov\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d
 /e/1FAIpQLSccsjcMG1SzdWI9GTNKlvV_ryO3mMXFYHjgrWwYwT1R_U1-0g/viewform?usp=h
 eader\n\nJoin Marci Kwon\, Exhibition Co-Curator & Co-director of the AAAI
 \, on this special tour of surfacing.  \n\nRSVP HERE\n\npatty chang: surfa
 cing engages the ocean as a physical\, geopolitical\, and symbolic space. 
 The exhibition culminates a year-long residency through the Denning Visiti
 ng Artist program\, during which Chang was embedded at Stanford’s Hopkin
 s Marine Station. Incorporating fish specimens\, archaeological remains\, 
 archival materials documenting the lives of Chinese fisher families in the
  early 1900s\, and a porcelain table that travels from the Metropolitan Mu
 seum of Art to take new form at the Anderson\, Chang’s sculptural practi
 ce surfaces the mysterious intimacies and unrecorded histories that haunt 
 the Pacific Ocean and its coast. surfacing is the first solo artist exhibi
 tion commission for Stanford’s Asian American Art Initiative (AAAI). \n\
 nThe exhibition will be on view in the Wisch Family Gallery from September
  17\, 2026 – February 8\, 2027.
END:VEVENT
