URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/curator-led-talk-surfacing-feb
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53756115803602.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/cura
 tor-led-talk-surfacing-feb\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d
 /e/1FAIpQLSftIcUgvsEFDBmPbKXiAFiKnkydy7locRoYqCZpw1L-DoaQzw/viewform?usp=h
 eader\n\nJoin Kelsey Chen\, Exhibition Co-Curator\, on this special tour o
 f surfacing.  \n\nRSVP HERE\n\npatty chang: surfacing engages the ocean as
  a physical\, geopolitical\, and symbolic space. The exhibition culminates
  a year-long residency through the Denning Visiting Artist program\, durin
 g which Chang was embedded at Stanford’s Hopkins Marine Station. Incorpo
 rating fish specimens\, archaeological remains\, archival materials docume
 nting the lives of Chinese fisher families in the early 1900s\, and a porc
 elain table that travels from the Metropolitan Museum of Art to take new f
 orm at the Anderson\, Chang’s sculptural practice surfaces the mysteriou
 s intimacies and unrecorded histories that haunt the Pacific Ocean and its
  coast. surfacing is the first solo artist exhibition commission for Stanf
 ord’s Asian American Art Initiative (AAAI). \n\nThe exhibition will be o
 n view in the Wisch Family Gallery from September 17\, 2026 – February 8
 \, 2027.
