DTSTART:20261108T020000Z
DTEND:20261108T020000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] 16th Bita Prize for Persian Arts: Sima Bina
LOCATION:In person at Stanford
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/16th-bita-prize-for-persian-arts-cele
 brating-sima-bina
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53790868744168.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/16th
 -bita-prize-for-persian-arts-celebrating-sima-bina\n報名/票券: https:/
 /16th-bita-prize.eventbrite.com\n\nJoin us for the 16th Bita Prize for Per
 sian Arts celebrating acclaimed Iranian musician Sima Bina.\n\nSima Bina i
 s a renowned Iranian folk singer\, songwriter\, and researcher. She is cel
 ebrated for her contributions to preserving and promoting Persian folk mus
 ic and culture.\n\nSima Bina was born in 1945\, in Khorasan\, Iran. Her pa
 ssion for folk music emerged from her childhood experiences\, as she grew 
 up surrounded by traditional Persian melodies and rhythms. She began singi
 ng at an early age and was particularly drawn to the rich tapestry of regi
 onal folk songs from different parts of Iran.\n\nHer professional career g
 rew in the 1960s when she started performing publicly and recording albums
 . Bina's distinctive voice and her ability to interpret traditional songs 
 with authenticity quickly earned her recognition within Iran and abroad.\n
 \nBina is also a dedicated researcher and educator. Throughout her career\
 , Bina has tirelessly worked to collect\, document\, and preserve Persian 
 folk music\, traveling to remote regions of Iran to learn from local music
 ians and record their songs. She has amassed an extensive repertoire of fo
 lk songs representing various ethnic groups and regions of Iran\, from Kur
 dish lullabies to Baluchi melodies. She has published books on Persian fol
 k music and has lectured at universities and cultural institutions around 
 the world\, sharing her knowledge and passion for Iranian musical heritage
 .\n\nBina's impact on Persian folk music extends beyond her own performanc
 es
END:VEVENT
