DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53801235932031.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/lunc
 htime-curator-talk-california-current-art-and-histories-from-the-bay-area\
 n報名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/cacurrent1105\n\nJoin Alees
 a Pitchamarn Alexander\, the Robert M. and Ruth L. Halperin Associate Cura
 tor of Modern and Contemporary Art\, on this special tour of California Cu
 rrent: Art and Histories from the Bay Area.\n\nRSVP here.\n\nHow does a co
 mmunity stay rooted in a region that’s constantly changing? California C
 urrent invites you to consider this question and others through its more t
 han 60 works — many on view for the first time — that explore the inte
 rplay between Bay Area history\, art\, and artists over the past century.\
 n\nTitled after the major cold-water current that runs the length of the W
 est Coast of North America\, California Current brings together paintings\
 , sculptures\, works on paper\, photographs\, and time-based media by Bay 
 Area artists from the twentieth century to the present. The exhibition tra
 ces a series of interconnected currents — ecological\, infrastructural\,
  technological\, personal\, creative\, and political — that have shaped 
 both artistic production and everyday life in Northern California.\n\nArra
 nged thematically across time and media\, California Current places histor
 ical works in conversation with contemporary ones\, emphasizing both conti
 nuity and change. Together\, they ask: What has drawn so many people to th
 is region? What has allowed communities and creative practices to take roo
 t here? And what continues to keep so many of us — despite the Bay Area
 ’s contradictions\, pressures\, and constant reinvention — deeply conn
 ected to this place? Presented as part of the Further 
END:VEVENT
