SUMMARY:[線上] ENT Experts Up Close: Updates in Parotid Masses and Sinona
 sal Malignancies
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-experts-up-close-updates-in-parot
 id-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53809595903126.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/ent-
 experts-up-close-updates-in-parotid-masses-and-sinonasal-malignancies\n報
 名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=5
 7310\n\nOverviewThis one-hour CME activity offers a concise\, evidence-bas
 ed update on the evaluation\, diagnosis\, and management of parotid masses
  and sinonasal malignancies. Topics cover contemporary imaging\, pathology
  interpretation\, surgical approaches\, as well as adjuvant and systemic t
 herapies. The session emphasizes multidisciplinary decision-making\, funct
 ional outcomes (including facial nerve preservation and skull base conside
 rations)\, survivorship\, and select endoscopic and minimally invasive tec
 hniques. Attendees will leave with useful takeaways to support clinical de
 cision-making\, streamline referrals\, and stay current on evolving treatm
 ent options and clinical trials.\n\nRegistrationRegistration for all pract
 itioners - free\n\nTo register for this activity\, please click HERE.\n\nC
 reditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participa
 tion Credit (1.00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Allergy\, Immunol
 ogy\, and Rheumatology\, Otolaryngology (ENT)Professions - Advance Practic
 e Nurse (APN)\, Fellow/Resident\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Physician\, Regi
 stered Nurse (RN)\n ObjectivesAt the conclusion of this activity\, learner
 s should be able to:\n1. Describe types of molecular testing available for
  parotid masses \n2. Review the contraindications and indications for paro
 tidectomy\n3. Identify updates in diagnostic workup and staging criteria f
 or sinonasal malignancies\n4. Describe emerging systemic therapies and act
 ive clinical trials relevant to sinonasal cancer management\n\nAccr
END:VEVENT
