SUMMARY:[現場] Reading with Robin Coste Lewis\, the Mohr Visiting Poet
LOCATION:Faculty Club\, Cedar Room
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/reading-with-robin-coste-lewis-the-mo
 hr-visiting-poet
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53853582945229.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/read
 ing-with-robin-coste-lewis-the-mohr-visiting-poet\n\nThe Creative Writing 
 Program is pleased to announce the next event with the Mohr Visiting Poet:
  A Reading with Robin Coste Lewis.\n\nThis event is open to Stanford affil
 iates and the general public. Registration is encouraged but not required\
 ; RSVP form to follow.\n\n____\n\nRobin Coste Lewis is a writer and artist
 . Lewis won the National Book Award for Voyage of the Sable Venus\, he
 r first collection of poetry. The book was also a finalist for the Hurston
 /Wright Legacy Award and the Los Angeles Times Book Award\, and it was
  named one of the best books of the year by The New Yorker and The N
 ew York Times. Literary Hub named it one of the best books of the last t
 wenty years. Lewis was the first African-American to ever win the National
  Book Award in a debut\, and the first woman to do so since 1974. Her seco
 nd book\, To the Realization of Perfect Helplessness\, was the winner of
  the PEN/Voelcker Award for Poetry and the NAACP Image Award for Outstandi
 ng Literary Work in Poetry. She is also the coauthor\, with Kevin Young\, 
 of Robert Rauschenberg: Thirty-Four Illustrations for Dante’s Inferno\
 , published by the Museum of Modern Art. Her latest book\, Archive of 
 Desire\, was named by the Brooklyn Public Library as one of the best poetr
 y collections of the year. The former poet laureate of Los Angeles\, Lewis
  holds a PhD in poetry and visual studies from the University of Southern 
 California\, an MFA in poetry from New York University\, an MTS in Sanskri
 t and comparative religious literature from t
END:VEVENT
