SUMMARY:[現場] Reading with Jenny Tinghui Zhang\, the Stein Visiting Writ
 er
LOCATION:Bechtel Conference Center\, Main Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/reading-with-jenny-tinghui-zhang-the-
 stein-visiting-writer
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53853624342649.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/read
 ing-with-jenny-tinghui-zhang-the-stein-visiting-writer\n\nThe Creative Wri
 ting Program is pleased to announce the next event with the Stein Visiting
  Writer: A Reading with Jenny Tinghui Zhang.\n\nThis event is open to Stan
 ford affiliates and the general public. Registration is encouraged but not
  required\; RSVP form to follow.\n\n____\n\nJenny Tinghui Zhang is the nat
 ionally bestselling author of the novels Superfan and Four Treasures of th
 e Sky\, named an Idaho Book of the Year and short- and longlisted for the 
 Chautauqua Prize\, the Dublin Literary Award\, the Carnegie Medal for Exce
 llence in Fiction\, and the VCU Cabell First Novelist Award. A National Bo
 ok Foundation 5 Under 35 Honoree\, she has received support from Hedgebroo
 k\, Yaddo\, and Kundiman\, among others. Her work has appeared in Vogue\, 
 Elle\, Foreign Policy\, The New York Times\, and elsewhere. She lives in A
 ustin\, Texas.\n\n____\n\nZhang is this year's Stein Visiting Writer. Each
  year\, the Creative Writing Program welcomes distinguished writers to hos
 t events and teach a Stanford writing seminar to undergraduates. These eve
 nts and seminars are made possible with the generous support of Isaac and 
 Madeline Stein.\n\n____\n\nNo personal recordings (audio or visual) are al
 lowed. By attending\, you consent for your image to be used for Stanford-r
 elated promotions and materials. If you have any questions\, please contac
 t ethics-center@stanford.edu \n\nIf you require disability-related accommo
 dation\, please contact disability.access@stanford.edu as soon as possible
  or at least 7 business days in advanc
END:VEVENT
