SUMMARY:[線上] Open Wide the Doors: The Prison Memoirs of Mahvash Sabet
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/open-wide-the-doors-the-prison-memoir
 s-of-mahvash-sabet
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53859860302680.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/open
 -wide-the-doors-the-prison-memoirs-of-mahvash-sabet\n報名/票券: https:
 //stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ZyvUqvrWTW22x4eJHWMkBw\n\nIn 2018\,
  during her brief respite of freedom between two decade-long prison senten
 ces\, Mahvash Sabet asked Bahiyyih Nakhjavani and Azita Mottahedeh to work
  on her memoirs and make a book that could convey her story in English. Th
 ey set to work\, with Mottahedeh translating the Persian original\, word f
 or word\, and Nakhjavani attempting to structure a narrative from the more
  than 750 pages of a harrowing and uplifting testimony which Sabet smuggle
 d out of prison over the years.\n\n“In this discussion\, we will explore
  the decisions involved and the methods followed in the course of creating
  this book\, as well as the distinctive characteristics of Mahvash Sabet's
  style\, tone and intent\, which we hope have survived the translation.  W
 e will share the ways in which this prison memoir may be different from ot
 hers and at the same time how it seems to bear witness to the many which m
 ight never be written.  Above all we will try to share Mahvash’s extraor
 dinary capacity to transform despair into hope\, confinement into freedom\
 , and estrangement and isolation into a boundless compassion towards other
 s.”\n\nBahiyyih Nakhjavani was born in Iran\, raised in Uganda\, and edu
 cated in the UK and the US. She received her preliminary degrees in Englis
 h Literature from the University of York in the UK\, and completed her doc
 torate at UMass\, Amherst\, in the US\, as well as being awarded an honora
 ry doctorate by the University of Liège in Belgium. In addition to teachi
 ng literature and creative writing over
END:VEVENT
