SUMMARY:[混合] HAI Seminar with Marcos Santiago Rojas Pino & Thomas Carus
 o
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-seminar-with-marcos-santiago-roja
 s-pino-thomas-caruso
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53861067888210.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-
 seminar-with-marcos-santiago-rojas-pino-thomas-caruso\n線上連結: https
 ://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_t0MhcVbrT1SZSPDHBHBw5g#/registrati
 on\n報名/票券: https://hai.stanford.edu/events/marcos-santiago-rojas-p
 ino-thomas-caruso-building-an-international-ai-platform-for-health-profess
 ions-education-and-the-learning-sciences\n\nClinical Mind AI: Building an 
 International AI Platform for Health Professions Education and the Learnin
 g Sciences\n\nHAI Seminar with Marcos Santiago Rojas Pino and Thomas Carus
 o\n\nVisit our website to learn more about the event agenda\, speakers\, a
 nd other details\n\nClinical Mind AI is a Stanford-developed\, internation
 al collaborative platform designed to strengthen clinical reasoning educat
 ion through AI-simulated patient encounters across health professions. The
  platform enables educators to create clinical cases aligned with their lo
 cal curricula\, learning goals\, languages\, and assessment needs\, while 
 giving learners repeated opportunities to practice open-ended history-taki
 ng\, diagnostic reasoning\, and communication. The seminar will present th
 e motivation for Clinical Mind AI\, its design principles\, and how the pl
 atform is being used by educators and institutions across countries to sup
 port scalable\, instructor-centered clinical simulation.\n\nThe talk will 
 also discuss Clinical Mind AI as a research infrastructure for studying le
 arning in clinical reasoning tasks. We will describe how learner interacti
 ons with AI-simulated patients can generate interpretable evidence about r
 easoning processes\, including how students gather information\, update hy
 potheses\, document findings\, and respond to feedback. The seminar will f
 ocus on broader questions at the intersection of AI\, medical education\, 
 and learning science: how to build AI systems that preserve instructor age
 ncy\, support mul
END:VEVENT
