SUMMARY:[混合] HAI Seminar The AI 100
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-seminar-with-mike-wooldridge-the-
 ai-100
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53861242574668.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-
 seminar-with-mike-wooldridge-the-ai-100\n線上連結: https://stanford.zo
 om.us/webinar/register/WN_OeOA7YGwQ8qGOfBdrTXx6w#/registration\n報名/票
 券: https://hai.stanford.edu/events/mike-wooldridge-the-ai-100\n\nAI Goes
  Mainstream: The Scaling Era and the Rise of Generative AI\n\nMichael Wool
 dridge\, Ashall Professor of the Foundations of Artificial Intelligence\, 
 University of Oxford\n\nModerated by: Russ Altman\, Kenneth Fong Professor
  and Professor of Bioengineering\, of Genetics\, of Medicine\, of Biomedic
 al Data Science\, Senior Fellow at the Stanford Institute for Human-Center
 ed AI and Professor\, by courtesy\, of Computer Science\n\nThis talk will 
 cover key insights from the third AI100 report\, AI Goes Mainstream: The S
 caling Era and the Rise of Generative AI\, set for release in October 2026
 . The report was commissioned by the AI100 standing committee and led by s
 tudy panel chair Michael Wooldridge.\n\nWooldridge will discuss how genera
 tive AI achieved World Wide Web-level impact in five years\, largely unant
 icipated even by its developers\; why software engineering became AI's fir
 st killer app and what that suggests for knowledge work\; the unprecedente
 d scale of AI infrastructure investment and the strains it creates\; and t
 he shift away from pure scaling toward reasoning and inference-time comput
 e. He will also cover the concentration of frontier development among a sm
 all number of US and Chinese actors\, expert disagreement over AGI timelin
 es\, and a governance landscape that remains fragmented.\n\nThe One Hundre
 d Year Study on Artificial Intelligence (AI100) is a longitudinal effort a
 dministered out of Stanford HAI and managed by a standing committee of AI 
 experts from around the world\, chaired b
END:VEVENT
