SUMMARY:[混合] HAI Seminar with Angèle Christin in Conversation with Han
 nah Zeavin
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-seminar-with-angele-christin-in-c
 onversation-with-hannah-zeavin
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53861598502050.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/hai-
 seminar-with-angele-christin-in-conversation-with-hannah-zeavin\n線上連
 結: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_oNm5zUqVS5WO0JywL4KyTQ#/
 registration\n報名/票券: https://hai.stanford.edu/events/angele-christ
 in-hannah-zeavin-gurus-hucksters-entertainers-how-influencers-reshaped-soc
 ial-media\n\nBook Launch: “Gurus\, Hucksters\, Entertainers: How Influen
 cers Reshaped Social Media”\n\nHAI Seminar with Angèle Christin in Conv
 ersation with Hannah Zeavin\n\nVisit our website to learn more about the e
 vent agenda\, speakers\, and other details\n\nPlease join us for an illumi
 nating investigation of the complex work of social media content creators
 —their lives\, conflicts\, and controversies. \n\nIn this eye-opening bo
 ok\, digital studies scholar Angèle Christin demystifies the content crea
 tor economy\, explaining its long history and the pitfalls of its professi
 onalization. Drawing on in-depth fieldwork with digital creators as varied
  as vegan YouTubers\, dads of Instagram\, and self-described drama comment
 ators\, Christin shows how individuals enter social media creation\, how t
 hey make money\, and how their online environments shape their content.
END:VEVENT
