 public-events/e/54010921145793.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/copy
 -of-lunchtime-curator-talk-california-current-art-and-histories-from-the-b
 ay-area-282\n報名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/gPgMztAP\n\nJoi
 n Maggie Dethloff\, Assistant Curator of Photography and New Media\, on th
 is special tour of California Current: Art and Histories from the Bay Area
 .\n\nRSVP here.\n\nHow does a community stay rooted in a region that’s c
 onstantly changing? California Current invites you to consider this questi
 on and others through its more than 60 works — many on view for the firs
 t time — that explore the interplay between Bay Area history\, art\, and
  artists over the past century.\n\nTitled after the major cold-water curre
 nt that runs the length of the West Coast of North America\, California Cu
 rrent brings together paintings\, sculptures\, works on paper\, photograph
 s\, and time-based media by Bay Area artists from the twentieth century to
  the present. The exhibition traces a series of interconnected currents 
 — ecological\, infrastructural\, technological\, personal\, creative\, a
 nd political — that have shaped both artistic production and everyday li
 fe in Northern California.\n\nArranged thematically across time and media\
 , California Current places historical works in conversation with contempo
 rary ones\, emphasizing both continuity and change. Together\, they ask: W
 hat has drawn so many people to this region? What has allowed communities 
 and creative practices to take root here? And what continues to keep so ma
 ny of us — despite the Bay Area’s contradictions\, pressures\, and con
 stant reinvention — deeply connected to this place? Presented as part of
  the Further Triennial\, this exhibition features works by arti
END:VEVENT
