SUMMARY:[現場] "Tracing Mindfulness Back to Its Sources": T. T. and W. F.
  Chao Workshop with Bhikkhunī Dhammadinnā and Paul Harrison
LOCATION:Alumni Center\, McCaw Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/tracing-mindfulness-back-to-its-sourc
 es-t-t-and-w-f-chao-workshop-with-bhikkhuni-dhammadinna-and-paul-harrison
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53870838804293.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/trac
 ing-mindfulness-back-to-its-sources-t-t-and-w-f-chao-workshop-with-bhikkhu
 ni-dhammadinna-and-paul-harrison\n\nThis workshop is a part of the T. T. &
  W. F. Chao Buddhism and Contemporary Society Series and will explore the 
 early Buddhist sources of mindfulness meditation in theory and in practice
 . Participants will be guided through an examination of the teachings that
  form the shared inheritance of all later Buddhist traditions and that als
 o inform many contemporary applications. Throughout the day\, we will be l
 ooking into multiple constructs and perspectives on mindfulness and their 
 practical implications\, discovering how theory\, practice\, and their int
 erweaving have continually evolved—shaped by diverse maps and goals of t
 he Buddhist path across time\, through different cultures\, and into prese
 nt-day recontextualizations.\n\n​The workshop will offer participants th
 e opportunity for experiential exploration of the relevant practices toget
 her with an accessible scholarly grounding in the primary textual sources 
 in translation.\n\n​This event is free and open to the public\, and ever
 yone is welcome. However\, because of space limitations\, registration is 
 essential. Registration will close on November 10. Some prior exposure to 
 basic Buddhist or mindfulness teachings and practices is helpful but not a
  prerequisite for participation.\n\nPlease register here. \n\n​Schedule:
 \n\n​Morning Session\n\n​09:00–09:10 Introduction\n\n​09:10–09:2
 0 Guided Meditation\n\n​09:20–10:00 The Four Foundations of Mindfulnes
 s (satipaṭṭhāna) in Theory & Practice: An Overview\n\n​10:00–10:3
 0 Discussion\n\n​10:30–10:45 Short Break\n\n
END:VEVENT
