  Shoshana Ungerleider
LOCATION:Cedar Room\, Stanford Faculty Club\, Cedar Room
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/36th-annual-jonathan-j-king-lecture
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53871308387148.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/36th
 -annual-jonathan-j-king-lecture\n線上連結: https://med.stanford.edu/bi
 oethics.html\n報名/票券: https://StanfordKingLecture.eventbrite.com\n\
 nThe Girand Center for Biomedical Ethics is pleased to announce this year
 ’s speaker\, Dr. Bryant Lin\, in conversation with Dr. Shoshana Ungerlei
 der\, for the 36th Annual Jonathan J. King Lecture.\n\nWe invite you to jo
 in us on Thursday\, November 5 at 5:30pm PT in the Cedar Room at the Stanf
 ord Faculty Club or via livestream for My Cancer Journey: Happiness and Sa
 dness\, Hope and Fear. \n\nIn this talk\, Dr. Lin will share a candid and 
 deeply personal reflection on living with terminal cancer. As a leading re
 searcher\, cancer advocate\, and patient\, he brings a rare perspective to
  the realities of serious illness\, clinical care\, hope\, and what it mea
 ns to live fully in the face of uncertainty. Joining Dr. Lin is Dr. Shosha
 na Ungerleider\, a physician\, journalist\, producer\, and leading voice i
 n compassionate\, patient-centered care. Together\, Dr. Lin and Dr. Ungerl
 eider will explore the emotional and practical dimensions of a cancer diag
 nosis—including fear\, purpose\, relationships\, and the ways we navigat
 e life-limiting illness with honesty and humanity.\n\nSpecial book launch 
 opportunity: In-person attendees will have the opportunity to purchase sig
 ned copies of Dr. Lin’s new book\, Sunshine: An Exploration of Living Wh
 en You Are Dying\, releasing November 10. Hors d’oeuvres and refreshment
 s will also be served following the program.\n\nWe hope to see you there! 
 \n\n \n\nAbout the speakers\n\nBryant Lin\, MD\, MEng is a primary care ph
 ysician\, educator and researcher. The cornerstone of Dr. Lin's work i
END:VEVENT
