 unity Health\, Gastroenterology\, Gastroenterology & Hepatology\, Hematolo
 gy\, Internal MedicineProfessions - Advance Practice Nurse (APN)\, Non-Phy
 sician\, Nurse\, Physician\, Physician Associate\, Registered Nurse (RN) O
 bjectivesAt the conclusion of this activity\, learners should be able to:\
 n1. Apply NIAAA clinical criteria and phosphatidylethanol testing to accur
 ately diagnose alcohol-associated hepatitis and distinguish alcohol-associ
 ated liver disease from MASLD.\n2. Use MELD rather than the Maddrey discri
 minant function to risk-stratify patients with alcohol-associated hepatiti
 s and identify candidates for corticosteroid therapy.\n3. Manage corticost
 eroid therapy appropriately\, including assessmen
END:VEVENT
