DTSTAMP:20261102T121040Z
DTSTART:20261106T180000Z
DTEND:20261106T190000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] Artificial Intelligence Regulatory & Policy Landscapes
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/artificial-intelligence-regulatory-po
 licy-landscapes
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53944527851152.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/arti
 ficial-intelligence-regulatory-policy-landscapes\n報名/票券: https://g
 odort.libguides.com/fridaychats\n\nDate and Time: 10–11AM\, Friday\, Nov
 ember 6\, 2026Location: Virtual (zoom link provided upon registration)Inst
 ructor: Danielle Gensch (State\, Local\, and International Government Libr
 arian)This seminar is part of The American Library Association's Governmen
 t Documents Roundtable (ALA-GODORT) Friday Chats series (https://godort.li
 bguides.com/fridaychats). Please register through the ALA-GODORT website t
 o receive the Zoom link.\n\nGenerative artificial intelligence is almost e
 verywhere we look\, and researchers are considering its role and impact in
  a wide variety of fields. Several international\, state\, and local organ
 izations provide policy and regulation repositories worth knowing about. D
 anielle Gensch\, State\, Local\, and International Government Librarian at
  Stanford University Libraries will provide a brief tour of OECD\, NCSL\, 
 NLC\, and other helpful tools in the government information librarian’s 
 kit. She will focus on key topics like data centers\, energy\, sustainabil
 ity\, and intellectual property. Please feel free to bring your own exampl
 es\, particularly for federal resources\, generally outside the scope of D
 anielle’s work and her slides.
END:VEVENT
