SUMMARY:[混合] Using AI to Find Sources
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing\, Velma Denning Room (120F)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-find-sources
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53944542458283.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/usin
 g-ai-to-find-sources\n報名/票券: https://appointments.library.stanford
 .edu/event/17626269\n\nDate and Time: 2–3PM\, Tuesday\, November 10\, 20
 26Location: Velma Denning Room (120F)\, Green Library & Virtual (zoom link
  provided upon registration)Instructor: Pauline Lewis (Reference and Instr
 uction Librarian)Are you using AI to find sources for your research projec
 t? Do you think you should be but aren't sure how? Join this workshop and 
 learn concrete tips about the possibilities and limitations of using GenAI
  to discover primary and secondary sources. We'll explore how to thoughtfu
 lly use LLMs in this critical phase of your research and how to pair these
  new tools with traditional methods of discovering and accessing sources. 
 \n\nPlease register to attend. Registration is exclusively open to current
  Stanford affiliates and will be offered on a first-come\, first-served ba
 sis. For those attending the in-person event\, please bring your Stanford 
 ID card or mobile ID to enter the library. Virtual attendees will receive 
 a Zoom link upon registration.
END:VEVENT
