DTEND:20261119T213000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Galicia's Promised City with Oskar Czendze
LOCATION:Building 200\, History Corner\, 307
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/galicias-promised-city-with-oskar-cze
 ndze
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/53950377018750.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/gali
 cias-promised-city-with-oskar-czendze\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.
 com/forms/d/1euIgnTpdatJ3oa1vsQCf_V0GapwEdC6A-0gqpPE_M68/edit\n\nBetween 1
 890 and 1914\, tens of thousands of Jews from Galicia—the easternmost cr
 ownland of the Habsburg Empire—made New York City their new home. Yet th
 eir distinct experience has often been overshadowed by national narratives
  centered on migration from the Russian Empire. Oskar Czendze (University 
 of Toronto) will explores how Galician Jews carried forms of regional and 
 supranational belonging shaped in East Central Europe into New York. \n\nW
 hen: Thursday | Nov 19 | 12:00pm  \n\nWhere: Bldg. 200 | Rm. 307\n\n      
         \n\nRSVP required. Lunch included with RSVP.
END:VEVENT
