 0\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe_cyQG7aKsG3uF
 aiS_fhqIS4Pa3NA3fd58ZEaP4NWJwCRtvw/viewform?usp=header\n\nThe Creative Wri
 ting Program is pleased to announce a reading with Stegner Fellows in Poet
 ry and Fiction: J.L. Chen and Heidi Kaloustian. \n\nThis event is open to 
 Stanford affiliates and the general public. Registration is encouraged but
  not required. Register here\n\n____\n\nJ.L. Chen was born in Shanghai\, l
 ived in New York for nearly a decade before making her home in Vancouver\,
  Canada\, where she writes most mornings and dances into the night. Workin
 g in both English and Chinese\, she has published poetry and personal essa
 ys in ARC Poetry\, Literary Review of Canada\, Tupelo Quarterly\, Northwes
 t Review\, PRISM International\, Queen's Quarterly\, subTerrain\, and more
 . A finalist for the 2025 Robert and Adele Schiff Award (Cincinnati Review
 ) and longlisted for the 2025 CBC Poetry Prize\, Chen holds an MFA from th
 e University of King's College and is at work on a poetry manuscript and a
  memoir. (Instagram @jlchenwrites)\n\nHeidi Kaloustian is a writer from Mi
 chigan. She holds an MFA from the Iowa Writers' Workshop\, where she was t
 he Fiction Editor of the literary journal The Iowa Review. She has been th
 e recipient of an Avery Hopwood Award in Fiction\, a Kresge Fellowship in 
 the Literary Arts\, and a Robert J. Schulze Memorial Fellowship for a firs
 t novel. She is currently at work on a novel and a collection of stories.
END:VEVENT
