BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54003952174869@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T121334Z
DTSTART:20261105T023000Z
DTEND:20261105T040000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] You Belong Here: A Student Workshop
LOCATION:Encina Commons\, Room 123
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/you-belong-here-a-student-workshop
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54003952174869.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/you-
 belong-here-a-student-workshop\n報名/票券: https://forms.gle/rYtTG5MQq
 8oxoR7A8\n\nYou Belong Here: A Student Workshop creates a supportive\, ref
 lective space for Black and African students to explore belonging\, build 
 confidence\, and strengthen connections across campus. Through guided conv
 ersation\, small-group reflection\, and brief skills practice\, participan
 ts will surface common experiences of self-doubt and imposter feelings whi
 le recognizing the accomplishments and resilience that brought them to Sta
 nford.\n\nFacilitators will introduce practical strategies for reframing n
 egative self-talk\, celebrating milestones\, and cultivating peer networks
  that sustain academic and personal well-being. The session is intentional
 ly participant-centered: attendees can choose their level of engagement\, 
 and confidentiality and mutual respect are emphasized.\n\nFaculty and staf
 f are invited to attend in a supportive role to listen\, learn\, and reinf
 orce institutional commitment to inclusive belonging\; their presence shou
 ld prioritize students’ voices and experiences. Whether you are seeking 
 reassurance\, connection\, or concrete tools to bolster confidence\, this 
 workshop offers a welcoming environment to reaffirm that you earned your p
 lace at Stanford and belong in this community.
END:VEVENT
