UID:stanford-54004138576452@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T121334Z
DTSTART:20261110T200000Z
DTEND:20261110T213000Z
SUMMARY:[混合] Protest and Politics in Turkey in the 70s
LOCATION:Encina Commons\, Room 123
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/protest-and-politics-in-turkey-in-the
 -70s
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54004138576452.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/prot
 est-and-politics-in-turkey-in-the-70s\n線上資訊:\nRegister for Zoom li
 nk: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019fafd2880c7c7f91ffa9589e8b28f0\n
 報名/票券: https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019fafd2880c7c7f91ffa9589
 e8b28f0\n\nProtest and Politics in Turkey in the 1970s: Echoes of Dissent 
 offers the first comprehensive academic study of Turkey’s protest cycle 
 during the 1970s. Drawing on an original dataset\, the book examines the i
 nteraction between collective action and state repression\, tracing the de
 velopment of leftist\, nationalist\, and Islamist movements throughout the
  decade. The book also analyzes how the 1980 military coup suppressed orga
 nized political activity and reshaped the political arena\, contributing t
 o the subsequent rise of political Islam and the country’s broader right
 ward shift. By connecting the political struggles of the 1970s to contempo
 rary debates over authoritarianism\, democracy\, and protest\, the study c
 ontributes to scholarship on social movements\, repression\, and political
  change.\n\nThis event is co-sponsored by CDDRL's Program on Turkey and th
 e Abbasi Program in Islamic Studies.\n\nABOUT THE SPEAKER\n\nSelin Bengi G
 ümrükçü teaches political science at Rutgers University. She received 
 her PhD from the University of Zurich. She previously taught at İzmir Uni
 versity of Economics and held visiting positions at Bielefeld University\,
  Sciences Po\, Paris 8\, and the European University Institute. Her resear
 ch focuses on social movements\, political parties\, the far right\, polit
 ical violence\, and Europeanization\, with an emphasis on Turkey. Her firs
 t book\, Protest and Politics in Turkey in the 1970s: Echoes of Dissent\, 
 was published by Routledge in 2026.
END:VEVENT
