SUMMARY:[現場] Artist Talk | Holographic Space\, a talk by Charles Ray
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center\, Cantor Eastman Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/charles-ray
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54004410021939.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/char
 les-ray\n報名/票券: https://thethirdplace.is/event/charles-ray\n\nJoin
  us for an artist talk with renowned sculptor Charles Ray\, followed by a 
 conversation with Patrick R. Crowley\, Associate Curator of European Art a
 t the Cantor.\n\nFor over fifty years\, Charles Ray has worked towards the
  limits of sculpture\, exploring how the transformation of space can chang
 e a viewer's relationship to an object. Ray will reflect on his work over 
 the decades\, including his 16mm film Fashions (1996)\, which is currently
  on view in Solid Pictures.\n\nCurated by Patrick R. Crowley\, Solid Pictu
 res is the first major exhibition to explore the overlooked 1859 photoscul
 ptures of French artist and inventor François Willème\, whose experiment
 s translating photographic negatives into three-dimensional figures lay th
 e groundwork for modern 3D scanning and printing technologies.\n\nCrowley 
 will join Ray in conversation to discuss how Ray’s broader practice conn
 ects to the questions in the exhibition around three-dimensionality\, cons
 umerism\, and how clothing and fashion sit within the perceptual understan
 ding of a figure.\n\nAll public programs at the Cantor Arts Center are alw
 ays free! Space for this program is limited\; advance registration is reco
 mmended. Those who have registered will have priority for seating.\n\n​R
 SVP here.\n\nAbout the Artist\n\nCharles Ray (b. 1953) grew up in Chicago 
 and moved to Los Angeles in 1981\, where he currently lives and works. His
  art has been featured in Documenta\, three Venice Biennales\, and six Whi
 tney Biennials\, and his sculptures have been the s
END:VEVENT
