DTEND:20261106T020000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] No Ideas But in Things
LOCATION:Clark Center\, Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/no-ideas-but-in-things
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54011243977907.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/no-i
 deas-but-in-things\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIp
 QLSckBOFpxwAE-7A_LymttsLYcVqQOUBbRasHkVB9KNl83rbiGw/viewform?usp=header\n\
 nNo Ideas But in Things\n\nFilmed and Directed by Lan A. Li\nProduced by P
 eter N. Miller\n\nShort Film Screening\,\nfollowed by a discussion with th
 e filmmakers\n\n"No Ideas But in Things" is an art film that asks what can
  only be known through touch\, making\, and the body. Drawing on footage f
 rom the Material Intelligence seminar at the American Academy in Rome\, wh
 ere scientists\, makers\, and humanists explored how to learn from materia
 ls in an age of words and algorithms\, the film uses Rome as an object of 
 inquiry and conversation as an instrument of research\, rather than a vehi
 cle for predetermined conclusions. In doing so\, it reimagines scholarly o
 utput beyond the book\, article\, and essay.\n \n\nNovember 5\, 4:30-6PM (
 Clark Center Auditorium)
END:VEVENT
