 als (Brill 2021) and Japanese Supernatural Tales (Penguin Classics 2026). 
 Since 2022\, he has been the “Yōkai Navigator” for the documentary se
 ries YOKAI: Exploring Hidden Japanese Folklore (NHK World).\n\nFabio Rambe
 lli is Distinguished Professor of Japanese Religions and Cultural History 
 and International Shinto Foundation Chair in Shinto Studies at the Univers
 ity of California\, Santa Barbara. His many publications include: Buddhas 
 and Kami in Japan (with Mark Teeuwen\, 2000)\, Buddhist Materiality (2007)
 \, The Sea and the Sacred in Japan (2018)\, Spirits and Animism in Contemp
 orary Japan (2019)\, Gagaku: The Cul
