 i-songs-of-the-japanese-supernatural\n\nA multimedia presentation of Japan
 ese art and live jazz by the Fumi Tomita Quartet.\n\n  Fumi Tomita\, bass\
 n  Carl Clements\, woodwinds\n  Jason Ennis\, guitars\n  Gary Fieldman\, d
 rums\n\nFumi Tomita is a jazz bassist\, composer\, educator\, and author. 
  His newest recording\, Yokai! Songs of the Japanese Supernatural will be 
 released in October 2026 on Origin records and was inspired by 19th-centur
 y woodblock prints of Yokai and other Japanese supernatural creatures deri
 ved from folklore.  The album will be supported by a Northeast tour during
  October and November.  His 2019 recording\, The Elephant Vanishes: Jazz I
 nterpretations of the Short Stories of Haruki Murakami\, was released to c
 ritical acclaim by Origin Arts records and was listed in the top ten recor
 ds of 2019 by Jazziz. His 2020 release Celebrating Bird: The Music of Char
 lie Parker was similarly received.   \n\nTomita was active on the New York
  city jazz scene for over fifteen years and has performed at venues all ov
 er the U.S. and Canada including recent appearances at the International S
 ociety of Bassists Conference in Ann Harbor\, Michigan in June 2023 and th
 e Jazz Education Network conference in New Orleans and a short tour of Geo
 rgia\, both in January 2024.\n\nAs an author\, his second book\, Introduct
 ion to Early Jazz: A Concise Introduction from Its Beginnings through 1929
 \, was published by State University of New York Press in February 2024 an
 d was a guest on The Buzz\, the podcast of the Jazz Journalist Association
 .  His first 
