SUMMARY:[現場] Artist Salon: North African Traditions\, New Music Creatin
 g a Concerto for Oud and Baroque Orchestra
LOCATION:Building 80\, 102
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/artist-salon-north-african-traditions
 -new-music-creating-a-concerto-for-oud-and-baroque-orchestra
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54072728872237.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/arti
 st-salon-north-african-traditions-new-music-creating-a-concerto-for-oud-an
 d-baroque-orchestra\n\nJoin us for an Artist Salon: North African Traditio
 ns\, New Music Creating a Concerto for Oud and Baroque Orchestra\, a free 
 public conversation presented by Philharmonia Baroque Orchestra & Chorale\
 , Stanford Live\, and Stanford's Department of African and African America
 n Studies.\n\nDiscover the story of the oud—the fretless\, pear-shaped l
 ute whose sound has shaped musical traditions across North Africa and the 
 Middle East for centuries and which is an ancestor of the modern guitar.\n
 \nComposer Tarik O'Regan and oud virtuoso Joseph Tawadros will take audien
 ces behind the scenes of a new piece O’Regan has composed for oud and Ba
 roque orchestra\, scheduled to premiere at Bing Concert Hall on February 7
 \, 2027.\n\nO'Regan\, whose music has been performed by leading ensembles 
 around the world\, will discuss the inspiration behind the work\, while Ta
 wadros—whose performances have introduced international audiences to the
  expressive sound of the oud—will share the instrument's rich musical tr
 aditions\, demonstrate its remarkable range\, and offer insights into brin
 ging this new composition to life. The conversation will be moderated by S
 tanford professor and acclaimed scholar Professor Matthew D. Morrison\, wh
 ose work explores music\, culture\, and identity.\n\nThe event also featur
 es live musical demonstration by Joseph Tawadros\, a performance by the St
 anford Middle Eastern Ensemble\, and an audience Q&A\, offering attendees 
 the opportunity to engage directly with the artists.\n\nDate: Tuesday Febr
 uary 
END:VEVENT
