DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54178976599441.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/appl
 ied-physicsphysics-colloquium-jo-dunkley-the-simons-observatory\n\nAbstrac
 t: The Simons Observatory\, a new millimeter-wave observatory in the Ataca
 ma\, is now gathering data. With its smaller telescopes we are seeking a p
 rimordial signal imprinted by gravitational waves generated in the early u
 niverse. Its largest telescope is measuring the finer scales of the CMB wi
 th increased sensitivity\, probing the initial conditions of the early uni
 verse as well as revealing the later-formed cosmic web of gas and dark mat
 ter through the gravitational lensing and Sunyaev Zel’dovich effects. It
  will map half the sky at arcminute resolution\, overlapping with a number
  of large-scale structure surveys including Rubin. By surveying half the s
 ky every couple of days\, we also hope to see new types of transient astro
 nomical events in millimeter-wavelengths.  I will talk about the current s
 tatus of SO\, and its science plans.\n\nJo Dunkley is the Joseph Henry Pro
 fessor of Physics and Astrophysical Sciences at Princeton University. She 
 works on the analysis and interpretation of cosmological observations. She
  is currently the Spokesperson for the Simons Observatory collaboration. P
 reviously she was a member of NASA's WMAP science team and a scientist on 
 the European Space Agency’s Planck satellite project\, and was the analy
 sis leader for the Atacama Cosmology Telescope. She is a Fellow of the Roy
 al Society.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54180690948197@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T122238Z
DTSTART:20261105T193000Z
DTEND:20261105T210000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] The Body as Monument
LOCATION:El Centro Chicano\, Jaime Miranda Lounge
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-body-as-monument
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54180690948197.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/the-
 body-as-monument\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQL
 SdAiJ9dXkNqtkRMdUe_UdICulKlKXMHSq0krQoMLzfc2wQ7tw/viewform\n\nChicana/o-La
 tina/o Studies and El Centro are thrilled to welcome Jess Sabogal\, a cuir
  Colombian - American muralistx and printmaker from San Francisco whose la
 rge-scale public artworks attempt to document and disrupt. \n\nIn this art
 ist talk\, Jess Sabogal maps a two-decade creative evolution\, expanding f
 rom the monumental scale of muralismo and printmaking into intimate self-p
 ortraiture and sculpture. Guided by the relationships and histories that s
 ustain their practice\, Sabogal examines the shifting weight of an artist
 ’s responsibility. They explore lineage\, radical representation\, and t
 he urgency of creating work for communities whose bodies and futures remai
 n at risk for erasure.\n\nFor the past 10 years\, Sabogal has consistently
  reinvented what it means to be a muralistx in a male-dominated medium. Sh
 e has continuously pushed the boundaries as an artist by utilizing her med
 ium for social change\, action and empowerment. Her murals have been commi
 ssioned by Facebook\, Google\, 20th Century Fox\, the University of Southe
 rn California\, the University of California\, The University of Arizona\,
  and The University of Utah among many others. Sabogal’s work has been f
 eatured in national and international news and media sources including CNN
 \, The Wall Street Journal\, The Huffington Post\, and the New York Times.
 \n\nPlease RSVP ~ lunch will be provided!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54181164266640@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261007T235427Z
DTSTART:20270122T220000Z
DTEND:20270123T014500Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Arts +AI in the Evolving Research University
LOCATION:Jen-Hsun Huang Building (School of Engineering)\, Mackenzie Room (
 3rd floor)
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/arts-ai-in-the-evolving-research-univ
 ersity
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54181164266640.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/arts
 -ai-in-the-evolving-research-university\n\nJoin faculty members from Stanf
 ord and MIT for presentations and discussions on centering the arts as a c
 ore component of the research university's response to paradigm-breaking a
 dvances in AI.  How does art engage what most makes us human\, and does AI
  change the equation? How will the arts drive the evolution of higher educ
 ation that AI demands? How will arts integration save research universitie
 s from becoming institutes of applied AI?\n\n2:00 - 5:45PM\, reception to 
 follow.\n\n \n\nAdditional details coming soon
END:VEVENT
