SUMMARY:[現場] Estonia at the Front Line: Security\, Resilience\, and Tec
 hnology: A Discussion with the Prime Minister of Estonia Kristen Michal
LOCATION:Hohbach Hall\, Room 122
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/prime-minister-estonia-2026
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54188038982367.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/prim
 e-minister-estonia-2026\n報名/票券: https://forms.gle/jPeqBkywysHrXzAt
 7\n\nJoin us for an engaging discussion with Prime Minister of the Republi
 c of Estonia Kristen Michal on:\n\nEstonia at the Front Line: Security\, R
 esilience\, and Technology: Security\, Europe\, and Technology\n\nEstonia 
 sits at the intersection of some of the defining challenges of our time. B
 ordering Russia and on NATO’s eastern flank\, Estonia has had to make se
 curity and resilience a national priority. At the same time\, it has emerg
 ed as one of the world’s most digitally advanced societies. For Estonia\
 , security\, agility and innovation are not abstract ideas -- they are nec
 essities.\n\nIn this conversation with Estonian Prime Minister Kristen Mic
 hal\, we will explore what it means to lead a country on NATO’s eastern 
 flank at a time of profound geopolitical change\; why the outcome of Russi
 a’s war against Ukraine will shape Europe and the wider world\; and how 
 Europe can take greater responsibility for its own security.\n\nWe will al
 so discuss Estonia’s remarkable evolution into one of the world’s most
  advanced digital societies\, its ambitions in artificial intelligence\, a
 nd what smaller countries can teach us about adapting when new technologie
 s are reshaping economies\, governments and societies.\n\n\nThe discussion
  will be moderated by Michael McFaul\, Ken Olivier and Angela Nomellini Pr
 ofessor of International Studies\, Senior Fellow at the Hoover Institution
 \, at the Freeman Spogli Institute for International Studies and at the Wo
 ods Institute for the Environment.\n\nKristen Michal has served as 
END:VEVENT
