 drachkovitch-reopening-the-polich-room
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54188899938999.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/work
 -exile-and-home-honoring-milorad-drachkovitch-reopening-the-polich-room\n
 報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc7w217c3GK-oI_wL8
 HcB3tlPLmRGtzpr6egwlnr-YP6TgYtg/viewform?_hsenc=p2ANqtz--iyrx_UEYeXGvpRH4a
 OmRoWmcx0X802BFNNy1WbFrReEz27e4Qxkkmd82zDENq7FQwMA9D0mr84qZPYexRoltxeJe6tQ
 &_hsmi=2\n\nThis event will pay tribute to Milorad M. Drašković (Drachko
 vitch)\, who devoted more than three decades of his career to the Hoover I
 nstitution\, on the thirtieth anniversary of his passing. From 1974 to 198
 4\, Drašković led the Hoover Institution Library and Archives\, helping 
 to shape its vast collections and to support visiting researchers from aro
 und the world. He strengthened the ties between the Serbian\, Yugoslav\, a
 nd broader communities interested in the meaning of our shared history.\n\
 nAttendees will also enjoy exclusive access to the newly reopened Polich L
 ibrary (formerly the Polich Room)\, named in honor of Todor and Andja Poli
 ch. From 1968 to 2020\, the room hosted seminars and meetings with disting
 uished scholars and international visitors at the Hoover Institution. Toda
 y\, it carries that legacy forward as a space devoted to the study of the 
 history of Yugoslavia.\n\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS\nDennis Bark is an emeritus s
 enior fellow at the Hoover Institution.\n\nHe is the author or editor of n
 ine books\, including Reflections on Europe (1997)\, an edited volume to w
 hich he contributed the essay “The American-European Relationship: Refle
 ctions on Half a Century\, 1947–1997.” His most recent work is Europea
 ns and Americans Dancing in the Dark (2007). In March 1997\, he was awarde
 d the Knight’s Cross of the Order of Merit\, First Class\, by the Federa
 l Republic of Germany in recognition of his contributions to German-Americ
 an relations. In October 2001\, he received the Knight’s Cross of t
END:VEVENT
