UID:stanford-54223304319471@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T122413Z
DTSTART:20261110T200000Z
DTEND:20261110T210000Z
SUMMARY:[混合] Relational Intelligence (RQ): Building Relational Futures 
 in the Age of AI
LOCATION:Building 120\, McClatchy Hall\, Main Quad\, Studio S40 - bring you
 r Stanford ID card/mobile ID to enter the building
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/relational-intelligence-rq-building-r
 elational-futures-in-the-age-of-ai
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54223304319471.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/rela
 tional-intelligence-rq-building-relational-futures-in-the-age-of-ai\n線
 上連結: https://youtube.com/live/0FahuE94C3U?feature=share\n線上資
 訊:\nSign up for the webinar here: https://stanford.zoom.us/webinar/regi
 ster/WN_FhoD1uNcSEOf5dBb6-gZNg#/registration\n報名/票券: https://cvent
 .me/VE7w48\n\nJoin the Tech Impact and Policy Center on November 10th from
  12PM–1PM Pacific for a seminar with Isabelle Hau.\n\nStanford affiliate
 s are invited to join us at 11:40 AM for lunch\, prior to the seminar. The
  Fall Seminar Series continues through December\; see our Fall Seminar Ser
 ies page for speakers and topics. Sign up for our newsletter for announcem
 ents.\n\nAbout the Seminar:\n\nAs AI reshapes how we learn\, work\, and co
 nnect\, understanding and strengthening human relationships has become an 
 urgent scientific and societal priority. This session invites researchers 
 across disciplines to explore Relational Intelligence (RQ)\, our capacity 
 to build trust\, cultivate belonging\, navigate differences\, and form mea
 ningful connections. Together\, we will examine emerging scientific questi
 ons\, identify opportunities for interdisciplinary research\, and imagine 
 new ways to measure\, develop\, and strengthen relational capacities. How 
 might we build a future in which advances in artificial intelligence are m
 atched by advances in human connection?\n \n\nAbout the Speaker:\n\nIsabel
 le C. Hau is the executive director of the Stanford Accelerator for Learni
 ng\, where she brings together learning & brain science\, technology\, and
  innovation to advance effective\, inclusive\, and human-centered approach
 es to learning.\n\nPreviously an impact investor\, Isabelle led the U.S. e
 ducation practice at Omidyar Network and Imaginable Futures\, investing in
  mission-driven organizations that have reached millions of learners. 
END:VEVENT
