SUMMARY:[現場] Emerging String Quartet Program – The Dolphins
LOCATION:Braun Music Center\, Campbell Recital Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/esqp-dolphins-quartet
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54231141268808.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/esqp
 -dolphins-quartet\n\nThe Dolphins Quartet performs as part of the Emerging
  String Quartet Program (ESQP).\n\nThe Dolphins Quartet is a string quarte
 t and composer collective united by a belief that chamber music can be vib
 rant\, daring\, and deeply human. Trained at Juilliard and based in New Yo
 rk City\, the quartet has gained recognition for adventurous programming\,
  original compositions\, and performances that reimagine the possibilities
  of quartet playing. In April 2026\, they won Gold Prize and Audience Priz
 e at the Chesapeake Chamber Music Competition\, establishing their presenc
 e as a world-class ensemble in the classical music scene. Read more here!\
 n\n \n\nMembers:\nLuke Henderson – violin\nIsaac Park – violin\nJames 
 Preucil – viola\nIan Maloney – cello\n\nThe ESQP provides a young ense
 mble opportunities similar to what the St. Lawrence String Quartet\, ensem
 ble in residence at Stanford University from 1998-2024\, enjoyed in their 
 early years through an intensive week of community outreach. The up-and-co
 ming musicians gain valuable experience performing for varied audiences in
  a short period of time while the greater Stanford community benefits from
  the input of energy and contact with the young ensemble.\n\nAmission Info
 rmation\n\nFree admissionParking permits are required for weekday campus p
 arking. We recommend downloading the ParkMobile app before arriving.
END:VEVENT
