 m/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=60458\n\nOverviewThis lecture will provide
  an overview of pediatric lower extremity development\, helping learners d
 istinguish physiologic variations from pathologic findings. Learners will 
 review common causes of in-toeing gait\, develop strategies for identifyin
 g the source of rotational deformities through physical examination\, and 
 recognize red flags in gait and lower extremity alignment. The session wil
 l also provide practical guidance for counseling families about expected n
 atural history and determining when further intervention is warranted.\n\n
 RegistrationRegistration is required.\n\nAll practitioners: free.\n\nCredi
 tsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ (1.00 hours)\, BOC Category A Hours/CEUs (
