 al Therapy Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, Physical Therapy Contact Hours (1.
 00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Orthopedics & Sports Medicine\, 
 PediatricsProfessions - Athletic Trainer\, Fellow/Resident\, Non-Physician
 \, Occupational Therapist\, Physical Therapist\n ObjectivesAt the conclusi
 on of this activity\, learners should be able to:\n1. Review pediatric low
 er extremity alignment and differentiate physiologic from pathologic. \n2.
  Discuss the most common causes of in-toeing gait in children and identify
  the source of rotational deformity through physical exam. \n3. Identify r
 ed flags in gait and lower extremity alignment. \n4. Counsel families on n
 atural history and indications for further intervention. \n\nAccreditation
 In support of imp
