SUMMARY:[線上] Holding the Line: Setting Boundaries for Yourself and Othe
 rs This Holiday Season
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/holding-the-line-setting-boundaries-f
 or-yourself-and-others-this-holiday-season
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54239642831812.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/hold
 ing-the-line-setting-boundaries-for-yourself-and-others-this-holiday-seaso
 n\n報名/票券: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5
 &EID=60415\n\nOverviewThe holiday season can bring a particular kind of pr
 essure for families caring for a child with medical complexity or navigati
 ng life after loss — from well-meaning relatives who don't understand ca
 re routines to social obligations that feel impossible to meet. This sessi
 on brings together a panel of parents\, some currently caregiving and some
  bereaved\, to talk honestly about what it looks like to protect your time
 \, energy\, and peace during this time of year. Panelists will share how t
 hey've learned to say no\, to ask for the support they actually need\, and
  to hold firm boundaries with extended family\, friends\, and even well-in
 tentioned strangers. The conversation will also explore the added layer be
 reaved parents carry — navigating traditions\, invitations\, and other p
 eople's expectations of grief — while still honoring their own family's 
 story. Join Courageous Parents Network for a candid\, supportive discussio
 n offering practical language and permission to protect what matters most 
 this season.\n\nRegistrationRegistration for all practitioners - free\n\nT
 o register for this activity\, please click HERE.\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Catego
 ry 1 Credits™ (1.00 hours)\, ACPE Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, ANCC Cont
 act Hours (1.00 hours)\, APA Continuing Education credits (1.00 hours)\, A
 SWB Continuing Education (ACE) credits (1.00 hours)\, CDR Continuing Profe
 ssional Education Units (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit 
 (1.00 hours)\, Occupational Therapy Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, Phy
END:VEVENT
