 public-events/e/54241742759378.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/film
 maker-kahlil-joseph-in-conversation\n報名/票券: https://luma.com/shf38
 g4b\n\nKahlil Joseph on the Representation of Space and the Making of the 
 Underground Museum\n\nJoin acclaimed filmmaker and artist Kahlil Joseph fo
 r a public conversation exploring the representation of space in his films
 \, including the construction of Black space in his latest feature-length 
 work\, BLKNWS: Terms and Conditions. \n\n\nThis event is part of the Art a
 nd Art History Course An Architectural Imagination taught by Christian Ho 
 as well as part of the ongoing work by Kahlil Joseph\, BLKNWS on view as p
 art of the permanent collection at the Harmony House\, home of the Institu
 te for Diversity in the Arts. \n\nWhen: November 10\, 2026\, 7:30–8:30 p
 .m. \nWhere: Oshman Hall\, McMurtry Art Building. \n\nPresented by: Depart
 ment of Art and Art History Institute for Diversity in the Arts Department
