SUMMARY:[現場] Artist Talk with CFGNY: A Practice in Collaboration
LOCATION:Anderson Collection\, The Denning Family Resource Center
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/artist-talk-with-cfgny-a-practice-in-
 collaboration
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54250092428311.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/arti
 st-talk-with-cfgny-a-practice-in-collaboration\n報名/票券: https://doc
 s.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSePvIBLF2R7SOI5P-HkmUzFG23gEpbrrmbqRCMWP9Q8S
 aT0OA/viewform?usp=header\n\nPlease join us for a roundtable discussion wi
 th CFGNY (Concept Foreign Garments New York) — an artist collective whos
 e multidisciplinary practice combines image making\, installation\, perfor
 mance and garment making — moderated by artist Vincent Chong ('26). The 
 collective uses materials such as porcelain\, stuffed animals\, photograph
 y\, drawing\, and corrugated cardboard to investigate notions of mass prod
 uction\, and fetishistic desire. At the heart of these investigations\, As
 ian identity fractures and fragments into what the collective refers to as
 \, “vaguely Asian.” \n\nRSVP HERE\n\nPanelists\n\nCFGNY is an artist c
 ollective whose research-based practice takes the form of image making\, i
 nstallation\, sculpture\,garment making\, and performance to expand ideas 
 of racialization and subjectivity. Founded in 2016\, the collective contin
 ually returns to the term “vaguely Asian”: an understanding of racial 
 identity as a specific cultural experience that includes being perceiv
 ed as other.\n\nRecent and upcoming exhibitions\, performances and project
 s include the 82nd Whitney Biennial\, New York (2026)\; Contemporary A
 rt Gallery\, Vancouver (2025)\; Cooper Hewitt Smithsonian Design Museum\
 , New York (2024)\; Hammer Museum\, Los Angeles (2024)\; SculptureCent
 er\, New York (2023)\; PIN-UP/Marséll\, Milan (2023)\; Japan Society\
 , New York (2022)\; X Museum\, Beijing (2021)\; RISD Museum\, Providen
 ce (2019)\;and Stedelijk Museum\, Amsterdam (2018). In October 2024\, 
 CFGNY was named Frieze London’s Focus Stand Prize winner 
END:VEVENT
