SUMMARY:[現場] MRC Public Lecture: Tadashi Tokieda
LOCATION:GSB Knight - Arbuckle / Cemex\, Cemex Auditorium
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/mrc-public-lecture-tadashi-tokieda
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54251541115699.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/mrc-
 public-lecture-tadashi-tokieda\n報名/票券: https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeGj8Br_-rXKmiwkZ_h2qhBqgQqH5YwW1drPkYg8G9ajpl_ng/viewform\n
 \nIf planning to attend\, please submit an RSVP here.\n\nThe Stanford Math
 ematics Research Center presents Surprises from rubbing the wrong way\, a 
 lecture given by Tadashi Tokieda\, Professor of Mathematics at Stanford Un
 iversity\, as part of the MRC Public Lecture series.\n\nFriction\, stickin
 ess\, jamming . . . Don’t we frown on these conditions as spoilers of li
 fe? This lecture\, however\, will perform baffling experiments that pop ou
 t of these conditions\, and probe their subtle physics via simple mathemat
 ics. You’ll be able to enjoy many of the experiments with friends and fa
 mily as easy magic.\n\nTadashi Tokieda is starting his 10th year as a memb
 er of the Stanford math department\, after vagabonding across careers — 
 painter\, philologist\, precarious plumber\, physicist. He likes to collec
 t counter‑intuitive phenomena which he discovers\, designs\, or learns a
 bout from others\, and to share them in outreach\, e.g. via the YouTube ch
 annel Numberphile. T^2 spoke in that capacity at the quadrennial Internati
 onal Congress of Mathematicians 2018\, 2022\, 2026.\n\nThis lecture is fre
 e and open to the public.\n\nSee the full event poster here.\n\nYou can fi
 nd more information about speaker Tadashi Tokieda on the Stanford Math Dep
 artment website.
END:VEVENT
