DTSTAMP:20261102T122615Z
DTSTART:20261104T200000Z
DTEND:20261104T210000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] CREATE Webinar - Modality: A Case Study in Implementing AI
  in Clinical Practice
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/modality-case-study-implementing-ai-c
 linical-practice
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54251622417790.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/moda
 lity-case-study-implementing-ai-clinical-practice\n報名/票券: https://
 stanford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_I1t4vA50SfKKUcGDTQq1aQ\n\nJoin us on 
 November 4\, 12–1pm PT for a roundtable discussion exploring what it tak
 es to move an AI-enabled behavioral health tool from development into real
 -world clinical practice\, using Modality as a case study. Speakers from M
 odality\, clinical partner Cornerstone Treatment Facilities Network\, and 
 research partner Stanford University will discuss how teams build trust an
 d organizational buy-in\, integrate new tools into existing workflows\, an
 d navigate challenges related to adoption\, usability\, privacy\, safety\,
  and potential bias. The conversation will also highlight the roles of cli
 nical\, technical\, research\, and implementation partners\, lessons from 
 real-world deployment\, and ongoing efforts to understand engagement\, fid
 elity\, and impact over time - offering a behind-the-scenes look at what i
 t takes to move promising technology toward meaningful\, sustainable use i
 n practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54251654190408@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T122615Z
DTSTART:20261111T200000Z
DTEND:20261111T210000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] Mental Health Technology + Innovation Hubinar: Integrating
  AI into Virtual Reality for Mental Health Care (Panel)
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/integrating-ai-virtual-reality-mental
 -health-care
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54251654190408.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/inte
 grating-ai-virtual-reality-mental-health-care\n報名/票券: https://stan
 ford.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_Y3GhpEwnSK6pqqjhaTntVA\n\nJoin us on Nove
 mber 11th\, 12-1pm PT for a panel on "Integrating AI into Virtual Reality 
 for Mental Health Care".\n\nVirtual and augmented reality are increasingly
  being used to deliver exposure-based treatments for anxiety related disor
 ders\, trauma\, addiction\, and other mental health conditions. Advances i
 n artificial intelligence are now expanding what these technologies can do
 \, enabling more interactive\, adaptive\, and personalized therapeutic exp
 eriences. In this panel\, experts spanning clinical research and digital h
 ealth will explore the evolving role of AI in virtual and augmented realit
 y for mental health care. Panelists will share examples of AI-enabled tool
 s designed to address real-world clinical needs\, including interactive vi
 rtual characters\, personalized exposure environments\, and systems that c
 an adapt treatment based on patient response. \n\nThe discussion will exam
 ine where AI can meaningfully enhance therapeutic XR\, what aspects of hum
 an interaction and real-world exposure these technologies are unable to re
 plicate\, and how clinicians can remain appropriately involved as systems 
 become more adaptive. Panelists will also consider the guardrails needed f
 or responsible use\, the potential role of wearable data in personalizatio
 n\, and the practical challenges of moving promising tools from research a
 nd development into evidence-based clinical practice.
END:VEVENT
