 son-recital-rachel-willis-sorensen\n報名/票券: https://live.stanford.e
 du/s/event?EventID=32601\n\nSoprano Rachel Willis-Sørensen is joined by p
 ianist Tamar Sanikidze for a recital of late Romantic songs by Rachmaninof
 f\, Sibelius\, and Strauss\, along with dramatic 20th-century selections b
 y Korngold\, Kander\, and Previn. A regular presence at the Metropolitan O
 pera and an audience favorite at San Francisco Opera\, Willis-Sørensen ha
 s been hailed by the San Francisco Chronicle for her “heroic power and t
 enderness.” Especially noted as a Strauss interpreter\, she was recently
  honored with the Beverly Sills Artist Award and made her Carnegie Hall re
 cital debut.\n\nThe Shenson Recital Series is generously funded by the Ben
  and A. Jess Shenson Funds at Stanford University.\n\nAdmission Informatio
 n\n\nTickets: $16.00 – $95.04
