UID:stanford-54296267539166@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261021T002430Z
DTSTART:20261117T180000Z
DTEND:20261117T193000Z
SUMMARY:[線上] Using AI to Listen\, Learn\, and Act on Community Feedback
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/using-ai-to-listen-learn-and-act-on-c
 ommunity-feedback
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54296267539166.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/usin
 g-ai-to-listen-learn-and-act-on-community-feedback\n報名/票券: https:/
 /ssir.org/webinars/entry/ai-community-feedback\n\nMeaningful change begins
  with listening. Evidence shows that when we genuinely understand people
 ’s needs and act on what we hear\, we make better decisions that lead to
  better outcomes. So how can AI help nonprofits and foundations listen to 
 more people\, synthesize large volumes of data\, and respond more effectiv
 ely? Join SSIR and Feedback Labs for a 90-minute interactive session explo
 ring AI for feedback and listening at scale. \n\nBuilding on Feedback Labs
 ’ research and experience\, we’ll hear case studies from nonprofits an
 d foundations that are using AI to accelerate and scale listening without 
 losing the nuance\, trust\, and human connection that make listening meani
 ngful. Participants will discuss what’s working\, what’s not\, and wha
 t responsible AI-enabled listening can look like in practice. Whether you
 ’re already experimenting with AI for listening or just beginning to exp
 lore its potential\, you’ll leave with practical ideas and questions to 
 help you determine where AI can\, and can’t\, strengthen your organizati
 on’s feedback and listening practices. \n\nJoin this interactive 90-minu
 te program led by Alexis Banks\, Director of Learning and Operations at Fe
 edback Labs\, and Annie Grier\, Director of Community and Equity at Feedba
 ck Labs. \n\nYou can expect to: \n\nWalk away with an understanding of how
  to think about effective and responsible AI use in the context of communi
 ty listening.Learn from peers who are using AI to accelerate\, scale\, and
  strengthen their feedback processes.Iden
END:VEVENT
