UID:stanford-54311459867594@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261102T122904Z
DTSTART:20261105T013000Z
DTEND:20261105T043000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Stanford in Haus Cramer: A Berlin Microhistory - Book Laun
 ch and Reception
LOCATION:Humanities Center\, Levinthal Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/stanford-in-haus-cramer-a-berlin-micr
 ohistory-book-launch-and-reception
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54311459867594.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/stan
 ford-in-haus-cramer-a-berlin-microhistory-book-launch-and-reception\n\nPle
 ase join the DLCL Department of German Studies for the Stanford in Haus Cr
 amer: A Berlin Microhistory book launch. Featuring a presentation with edi
 tors Karen Ruoff Kramer and Cheryce von Xylander\, and Faculty Emeritus La
 rry Friedlander. Reception to follow. We are delighted to invite you to jo
 in us for a celebration of the book’s release and of the Stanford in Ber
 lin community on campus and beyond! The book\, published to mark the 50th 
 anniversary of the Berlin Bing Overseas Studies Program\, offers a deep di
 ve into the rich history of the program\, the house\, and the city. Throug
 h its vast collection of perspectives and materials\, it showcases Haus Cr
 amer as witness to Berlin modernity\, to Jewish-German life between the wa
 rs\, and as a refuge for those who lived\, taught\, and studied in its roo
 ms. Take a look at the Stanford Library’s Spotlight Exhibit and find the
  book at Stanford University Press. We look forward to the celebration and
  to bringing together Berlin communities past\, present\, and future! RSVP
  for the book launch here. Respond by October 26 to secure your spot - lim
 ited seating available!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stanford-54311544929707@didiowen
DTSTAMP:20261022T175451Z
DTSTART:20261117T010000Z
DTEND:20261117T023000Z
SUMMARY:[現場] Book Talk: Prof. Cécile Alduy in Conversation with Prof. 
 Josh Landy
LOCATION:Building 260\, Pigott Hall\, Rm 216
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-talk-prof-cecile-alduy-in-conver
 sation-with-prof-josh-landy
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54311544929707.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/book
 -talk-prof-cecile-alduy-in-conversation-with-prof-josh-landy\n\nThe French
  and Italian Department and French Speaking Worlds: Here and Now present: 
 A Book talk on D’abord ils sont venus chercher les mots [First They Came
  for Words]\, les Arènes\, 2026\, by Prof. Cécile Alduy\, in conversatio
 n with Prof. Joshua Landy. \n\nAn Author Caught Up by Her Subject\nA profe
 ssor of literature at Stanford and a discourse analysis scholar\, Cécile 
 Alduy has spent years analyzing how the far right wages its culture war. I
 n 2022\, in La Langue de Zemmour (Zemmour’s Language)\, she showed how t
 he presidential candidate was distorting concepts and history to short-cir
 cuit rational thinking and appeal to hatred and fear. Then\, on January 20
 \, 2025\, her research caught up with her brutally. At Stanford\, her life
  and work were upended\, like those of colleagues\, students and workers i
 n universities\, schools\, administrations\, and scientific labs nationwid
 e\, when the new administration unleashed terror and censorship on culture
  and science. In this first-person account\, she tells what the far right 
 does once in power\, day to day.\n\nA New Linguistic and Political Regime\
 n“Women\,” “climate crisis\,” “disability\,” “diversity\,”
  “Black\,” “equality\,” “gender\,” “social justice\,” “L
 GBT\,” “prejudice\,” “racism\,” “vaccine” ... These words\, 
 among others\, have been banned or blacklisted by the Trump administration
  since March 2025. Cécile Alduy conducts a gripping investigation into th
 is list\, which grew from a handful of demonized terms into over 480 flamm
 able ones through anticipatory 
END:VEVENT
