 public-events/e/54313507284050.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/supe
 rintelligence-or-super-stupidity-designing-ai-systems-for-human-flourishin
 g\n線上連結: https://youtube.com/live/0FahuE94C3U?feature=share\n線
 上資訊:\nSign up for the webinar here: https://stanford.zoom.us/webina
 r/register/WN_FhoD1uNcSEOf5dBb6-gZNg#/registration\n報名/票券: https:/
 /cvent.me/VE7w48\n\nJoin the Tech Impact and Policy Center on November 3rd
  from 12PM–1PM Pacific for a seminar with Pat Pataranutaporn.\n\nStanfor
 d affiliates are invited to join us at 11:40 AM for lunch\, prior to the s
 eminar.  The Fall Seminar Series continues through December\; see our Fall
  Seminar Series page for speakers and topics. Sign up for our newsletter f
 or announcements. \n\nAbout the Seminar:\n\nAs AI becomes woven into our d
 aily lives and social institutions\, we are becoming “cyborgs\,” exten
 ding our minds and capabilities through technology. But greater technologi
 cal capability does not automatically lead to greater human flourishing. H
 ow can we design AI that strengthens our ability to learn\, create\, conne
 ct\, and make thoughtful decisions? In this talk\, I will introduce an int
 erdisciplinary approach to building AI systems and studying their effects 
 on people. Through personalized AI prototypes and large-scale experiments\
 , my research explores how AI can both enhance and undermine human decisio
 n-making\, well-being\, relationships\, and sense of self. This work combi
 nes design\, engineering\, and qualitative and quantitative research to ad
 vance a science of human-AI interaction grounded in human flourishing. I w
 ill also explore how research can translate into real-world impact: from a
 n AI digital twin that supports long-term thinking and has reached users i
 n more than 100 countries\, to research that has helped shape legislation 
 protecting children from companion AI. Finally\, I will discuss our 
END:VEVENT
