DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54347981525802.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/day-
 of-the-dead-celebrations-day-3\n\nDay of the Dead Celebrations | Lecture b
 y Rubí Tsanda Huerta\n\nRubí is an internationally recognized writer\, p
 oet\, historian\, Indigenous interpreter\, and emerging actress from the P
 ’urhépecha community of Santo Tomás in the municipality of Chilchota\,
  Michoacán. She is the author of three bilingual poetry collections in Sp
 anish and P’urhépecha. Her most recent publication appeared in the anth
 ology La voluntad de la tierra\, edited by UNAM and the Instituto Cervante
 s de España.\n\nRubí will be hosted at the Stanford Humanities Center an
 d will lead a series of events in the context of the Day of the Dead.\n\nN
 ov 2\, 2pm: What do altars and dead mean for P’urhépecha communities? I
 ntimate conversation with students and members of the Queer Student Resour
 ce Center.\n\nNov 3\, 4-5pm: Conversation and Blessing with El Centro stud
 ents.\n\nNov 5\, 5–6:30 pm: Lecture\, Dead and Life Celebrations in P’
 urhépecha Communities at the Native American Cultural Center.
