SUMMARY:[混合] Special Seminar and Fireside Chat: Understanding Work Usin
 g AI
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building\, 119
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/special-seminar-and-fireside-chat-und
 erstanding-work-using-ai
DESCRIPTION:➕ 加到我的行事曆: https://didiowen.github.io/stanford-
 public-events/e/54411409617637.ics\nhttps://events.stanford.edu/event/spec
 ial-seminar-and-fireside-chat-understanding-work-using-ai\n報名/票券: 
 https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/event/special-seminar-and-fireside-cha
 t-understanding-work-using-ai/\n\nThe government has maintained crucial da
 ta infrastructure that allow jobseekers to find jobs\, employers to hire\,
  and researchers to predict the future of work. This infrastructure is tes
 ted by rapid changes brought about by AI\, and at the same time\, is empow
 ered by the use of AI.\n\nPhil Lewis from the National Center for O*NET De
 velopment will talk about data infrastructure the US Department of Labor p
 rovides and how AI is used to update it. A panel with Diyi Yang from the S
 tanford Computer Science Department and DEL’s Erik Brynjolfsson will dis
 cuss the opportunities of a new partnership between Stanford and the Natio
 nal Center for O*NET Development.
END:VEVENT
